<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Huahine</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Huahine is an island in the Leeward group of the Society Islands in French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polynesia">Polynesia</a>, made up of two parts, Huahine Nui and Huahine Iti, joined by a narrow channel. Settled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polynesians">Polynesians</a> perhaps a thousand years ago, it has one of the largest concentrations of marae in the Pacific, at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maeva">Maeva</a>. It remained an independent kingdom until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> annexed it in 1895.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/huahine.jpg" alt="Huahine" width="320" height="238" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HuahineISS006-E-38879.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
